and logistics, and automotive manufacturer industries. Kyndryl Holdings, Inc. was incorporated in 2020 and is headquartered in New York, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Martin J. Schroeter | Chairman & CEO | Age 61 | Compensation: $3.8M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 72K people. Revenue per employee of $210K ranks in the bottom quartile among Technology peers. Each employee generates $5K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $889 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 18\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Kyndryl Holdings, Inc. is a mid-cap technology business with a $3.7B market cap on $15.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -4% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome. Operating margins are expanding by +3.3pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at -2% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $340M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 2 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 4.79\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.4\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 5.7\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 8.3% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 2.2% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.1\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (11.3% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Technology peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Technology peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 9% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Technology ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (52% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 67% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 67% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Bull of the Day: Kyndryl Holdings (KD)","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/commentary/3035454/bull-of-the-day-kyndryl-holdings-kd?cid=CS-ZC-FT-bull_of_the_day-3035454","date":"2026-11-26","timestamp":1795680000.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Kyndryl Holdings, Inc. (KD) Just Flashed Golden Cross Signal: Do You Buy?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3034440/kyndryl-hold